INT. FAMILY KITCHEN - MORNING

Pancakes burn. Smoke curls from the pan. A cat watches from the refrigerator top.

Mum, ROSEMARY ALDRIDGE (40s, bathrobe, phone against her shoulder), flips a pancake. It lands on the floor. She leaves it.

Her son, BARNABY ALDRIDGE (10, school jumper, one shoe), sits at the table, staring at his cereal.

BARNABY
It's soggy.

ROSEMARY
(into phone)
Yes. I'm here. Hold on.

She covers the receiver.

ROSEMARY (CONT'D)
Barnaby, shoes.

BARNABY
I'm not going.

ROSEMARY
Barnaby.

BARNABY
I'm not going.

ROSEMARY
(into phone)
No, not you. Go on.

GRANDMA (V.O.)
(tinny, through the phone)
Rosemary, put the boy on. Put him on.

ROSEMARY
Mum, he's eating.

GRANDMA (V.O.)
He's not eating. I can hear he's not eating.

Barnaby's spoon clinks against the bowl. He pushes cereal in a circle.

ROSEMARY
Barnaby. Grandma wants a word.

He takes the phone. Holds it away from his ear like a dead fish.

BARNABY
Hi.

GRANDMA (V.O.)
Barnaby, my darling. Do you know what day it is?

BARNABY
Tuesday.

GRANDMA (V.O.)
It's your sports day, isn't it?

His shoulders hunch. The spoon goes still.

BARNABY
I'm not doing the race.

GRANDMA (V.O.)
Why not?

BARNABY
Because I always lose.

Rosemary stops with the spatula in the air. She looks at him. He looks at the table.

GRANDMA (V.O.)
Your grandfather lost every race he ever ran.

BARNABY
Really?

GRANDMA (V.O.)
Every one. He'd come in last and hold his arms up like he'd won. Everyone cheered. You know why?

BARNABY
Why?

GRANDMA (V.O.)
Because he was the only one who looked like he was enjoying it.

Barnaby lifts his head. A corner of his mouth moves.

BARNABY
Grandpa did that?

GRANDMA (V.O.)
Put your mother back on.

He hands the phone to Rosemary. She takes it, breath held.

ROSEMARY
Mum?

GRANDMA (V.O.)
Burn another pancake. He likes them burned.

Rosemary laughs, a wet cracked sound. She wipes her eyes with the back of her wrist.

ROSEMARY
I love you.

GRANDMA (V.O.)
Hush. Go and flip.

The line clicks. Rosemary puts the phone down on the counter. She picks up the burnt pancake from the pan, slides it onto a plate, and sets it in front of Barnaby.

BARNABY
It's black.

ROSEMARY
Eat.

He takes a bite. Chews. Nods.

BARNABY
It's okay.

He picks up his other shoe.

FADE OUT.
